                  "code": "67781-5",
                  "system": "http://loinc.org",
                  "display": "Summarization of encounter note"
                }
              ]
            },
            "title": "Synthesis"
          },
          {
            "text": {
              "status": "generated",
              "div": "<div xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1999/xhtml\">Dear colleague, I am writing to inform you about the hospital course of your 19-year-old female patient, admitted on 06/04/2005 with a known meningomyelocele. Upon admission, a thorough neurological assessment was performed, including physical examination and evaluation of motor and sensory function of the lower extremities. Imaging and laboratory studies were conducted to guide surgical planning. On 08/04/2005, surgical repair of the meningomyelocele was performed without intraoperative complications. Postoperatively, the patient received wound care, intravenous fluid replacement, and pharmacological pain management. An indwelling urinary catheter was placed given neurogenic bladder dysfunction. Physical therapy was initiated, and neurological rehabilitation was commenced prior to discharge. The patient was discharged on 11/04/2005 in stable condition. Please ensure close outpatient follow-up including neurological and urological monitoring. Do not hesitate to contact me for further information.</div>"
            },
